<title>FRANCE: SOCCER-STRUGGLING LILLE SACK COACH.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-STRUGGLING LILLE SACK COACH.</headline>
<dateline>LILLE</dateline>
<text>
<p>Struggling French first division side Lille sacked coach Jean-Michel Cavalli and replaced him with former manager Charly Samoy, the club said on Friday.</p>
<p>Samoy, 57, a former goalkeeper in the 1960s and coach at Belgium's Mouscron in the 1970s, will try to save Lille from relegation with seven rounds left in the first division league.</p>
<p>Lille lie 17th of 20 teams on 33 points, 32 points behind leaders Monaco. Four teams will be relegated at the end of the season.</p>
<p>Cavalli, 39, was appointed Lille coach in August 1995.</p>
